# PROCEDURES / TRIGGERS / JOBS

Do not create stored procedures, triggers, scheduled jobs or hidden database automation unless:
1. the user explicitly requests it, OR
2. an approved architecture/business document requires it.

If requested:
- explain purpose;
- identify affected objects;
- assess transaction behavior;
- assess recursion/reentrancy;
- assess performance;
- assess security;
- add tests;
- define rollback/recovery.

Never introduce a trigger merely to compensate for missing application design.
